We present two novel classes of polynomial sequences, $\{P_n(x)\}_{n\ge 0}$ and $\{Q_n(x)\}_{n\ge 0},$, defined respectively by the recurrence relations:
\begin{align*}
&P_0(x)=1,\quad P_1(x)=x,\quad P_{n+1}(x)=xP_n(x)-(n-1)x^2P_{n-2}(x),\quad n\ge 1,
\end{align*}
and
\begin{align*}
&Q_0(x)=1,\quad Q_1(x)=x,\quad Q_{n+1}(x)=xQ_n(x)-n x^2Q_{n-1}(x),\quad n\ge 1.
\end{align*}
These sequences are connected to powers of Legendre polynomials, to $n$-th powers of Chebychev polynomials of the second kind, and to the count of acyclic orientations for circulant and specific circulant-like graphs. Additionally, we have recently identified a link between $Q_n(x)$ and the number of vertex-transitive digraphs on $n$ vertices that are not anti-transitive. We further examine the relationships among the sequences $\{P_n(x)\}_{n\ge 0}$, $\{Q_n(x)\}_{n\ge 0}$, and the count of irreducible polynomials of degree $n$ over $\mathbb{F}_2$. Finally, we offer a combinatorial interpretation of $P_n(1)$ utilizing standard Young tableaux. The study concludes with an array of open questions. Keywords: Recurrence relations, Generating functions, Graph theory, Combinatorics, Polynomial factorization. 2010 Mathematics Subject Classification: 05A15, 05A19, 05C30, 11B83.

\begin{abstract}
This work establishes hypercontractive inequalities for the Gaussian measure on the unit ball and certain weighted Berman measures on the complex unit ball. We also provide corresponding isoperimetric inequalities.
\end{abstract}
\begin{abstract}
We examine the $L_p$ gradient for holomorphic functions defined on the complex unit ball. By comparing $L_p$ norms against weighted $L_q$ norms of the Bergman-Bochner (Laplace-Beltrami) operator applied to these functions, we derive specific instances of weighted hypercontractivity inequalities. Furthermore, we prove weighted isoperimetric inequalities, demonstrating that they are equivalent to weighted logarithmic Sobolev inequalities.
\end{abstract}
\begin{abstract}
We establish a family of weighted hypercontractive inequalities for the Gaussian measure on $\mathbb{C}^n$. These results rely on weighted isoperimetric inequalities, which we show are equivalent to weighted Gaussian Sobolev inequalities.
\end{abstract}
\begin{abstract}
We derive weighted Gaussian Sobolev inequalities, which are equivalent to weighted isoperimetric inequalities.
\end{abstract}
\begin{abstract}
We introduce a family of weighted logarithmic Sobolev inequalities, each equivalent to a corresponding weighted hypercontractive inequality.
\end{abstract}
\begin{abstract}
We prove a family of weighted $L_p$ inequalities for holomorphic functions on the complex unit ball. These inequalities are equivalent to weighted $L_p$ inequalities for the (Laplace-Beltrami) Lefschetz operator.
\end{abstract}
\begin{abstract}
We demonstrate that the standard logarithmic Sobolev inequality for the Gaussian measure on $\mathbb{C}^n$ is equivalent to the standard hypercontractive inequality for the same measure.
\end{abstract}
\begin{abstract}
We establish weighted logarithmic Sobolev inequalities for the Bergman space of holomorphic functions on the complex unit ball.
\end{abstract}
\begin{abstract}
We prove that the standard logarithmic Sobolev inequality for the Gaussian measure on $\mathbb{C}^n$ is equivalent to the standard $L_4$ hypercontractive inequality for the Laplacian.
\end{abstract}
